{
 "about": "MAPPING keys over every kind of source: subject.roles, a TOKEN PIP without a value, a HEADER PIP with and without one, a GENERAL PIP whose body is a list, one string, a number, null or [] or that answers 500 or 404, a FILTERED PIP, subject.permissions itself (whose value another MAPPING PIP gives), a permission scope inside and outside iterate, an undeclared name, subject.id, and keys without the subject. prefix. The MAPPING PIP grants PARITY_R28_P on the key's value and PARITY_R28_Q on the reader's role, so a failed key that takes the whole attribute away shows on Q as well. The DENY rule under PERMIT_UNLESS_DENY tells a failed decision (false) from an ended rule (true).",
 "resourceTypePrefix": "PARITY_SUITE_R28P_",
